In summary, the terms "common myeloid progenitor" and "pluripotent stem cell (bone marrow)" are related but not identical concepts. While they are both involved in hematopoiesis, they represent different stages and types of stem cells. Therefore, their relationship should be classified as "related" with a confidence level of 5.
